Now, it's time to deploy the app.

For that, follow the below steps.

1. Use 'pip freeze > requirements.txt' to mark 'streamlit' and it's dependencies in 'requirements.txt'. This will help us to install all the packages on the server at once.

2. Well, 'pip freeze' will list out all the packages for this app to work but '> requirements.txt' is to mark them in a file.

3. Now, you need just the files that are really for the web app. So, create a new folder with 'web.py', 'functions.py' and 'todos.txt'. Create an environment '.venv' and install 'streamlit'. Now, our environment is also ready.

4. You now need to create a '.gitignore' file to mark '.venv' & '.idea' because we do not want that on GitHub. Include this 'readme.txt' as well.

5. So, now create a new 'public' repo and name it 'todo-webapp'. Copy the URL ('https://github.com/karankaru68/todo-webapp.git' in our case) and attach that git account to push the changes.

6. Now, run the app again using 'streamlit run web.py' and open the button 'Deploy' at the top right corner. You need to sign-in to 'streamlit'. You should be signing in through GitHub account so that you have less steps selecting the repo and all.

7. Now the simple step is to write your details and select your main file 'todo-app/web.py' -> Click 'Deploy'.

8. The app URL: 'https://karankaru68-todo-webapp-todo-appweb-prod-vj6ohk.streamlit.app/'.